{"t": 1794119190.5559294, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502s \u2014 root cause found, patch in reports/export.py\n\nCause: upstream ledger (2026.11) started adding a `currency` field to every row. `export_rows` wrote CSV with a fixed `id, amount` schema, so csv.DictWriter raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` on every export -> 502.\nEvidence: CloudWatch `/ecs/reports-api` (eu-west-1): `ERROR export failed: ValueError ... 'currency'` + `INFO upstream ledger 2026.11 added currency to every row`. Reproduced locally with a row containing `currency`.\nFix: `fieldnames=[\"id\", \"amount\", \"currency\"]` \u2014 export no longer raises, no data dropped; legacy rows without the field still export (empty column).\nHeads-up: the export CSV now has a 3rd column. Please check any downstream importer that assumes 2 columns; revert is the same one-line fieldnames change if the contract must stay `id, amount`."}, "ok": true}
